      "text": "First, we identify the coordinates of the vertices of the equilateral triangle base \\(ABC\\). Assume that \\(A = (0, 0)\\), \\(B = (12, 0)\\), and \\(C = (6, -6)\\). The height of the prism is 16, so the coordinates of the vertices of the top face \\(DEF\\) are \\(D = (6, -22)\\), \\(E = (0, -16)\\), and \\(F = (12, -16)\\).\n\nNext, we determine the coordinates of the midpoints \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\):\n- \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\), so \\(X = \\left(\\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2}\\right) = (3, -3)\\).\n- \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\), so \\(Y = \\left(\\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2}\\right) = (9, -3)\\).\n- \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(DC\\), so \\(Z = \\left(\\frac{6+6}{2}, \\frac{-6-22}{2}\\right) = (6, -14)\\).\n\nNow, we calculate the lengths of the sides of triangle \\(XYZ\\):\n- \\(XY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = 6\\).\n- \\(YZ = \\sqrt{(6-9)^2 + (-14+3)^2} = \\sqrt{(-3)^2 + (-11)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 121} = \\sqrt{130}\\).\n- \\(XZ = \\sqrt{(6-3)^2 + (-14+3)^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 + (-11)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 121} = \\sqrt{130}\\).\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[ XY + YZ + XZ = 6 + \\sqrt{130} + \\sqrt{130} = 6 + 2\\sqrt{130}. \\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{6 + 2\\sqrt{130}}\\).",
