      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\), we first need to understand the coordinates of points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\), which are the midpoints of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) respectively in the right prism \\(ABCDEF\\) with base equilateral triangles of side length 12 and a height of 16.\n\nThe vertices of the base triangle \\(ABC\\) are \\(A = (0, 0)\\), \\(B = (12, 0)\\), and \\(C = (6, -6)\\). The midpoints \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) are:\n\\[ X = \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (3, -3) \\]\n\\[ Y = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (9, -3) \\]\n\\[ Z = \\left( \\frac{6+6}{2}, \\frac{-6+0}{2} \\right) = (6, -3) \\]\n\nNow we calculate the lengths of the sides of triangle \\(XYZ\\):\nThe distance formula between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2} \\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the distance \\(XY\\):\n\\[ XY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36} = 6 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the distance \\(YZ\\):\n\\[ YZ = \\sqrt{(6-9)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{(-3)^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{9} = 3 \\]\n\nFinally, we calculate the distance \\(ZX\\):\n\\[ ZX = \\sqrt{(3-6)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{(-3)^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{9} = 3 \\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[ \\text{Perimeter} = XY + YZ + ZX = 6 + 3 + 3 = 12 \\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
