      "text": "First, we need to determine the coordinates of the vertices of the prism \\(ABCDEF\\) and the points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\). We start by placing the prism in a coordinate system.\n\nAssume the base of the prism is an equilateral triangle \\( \\triangle ABC \\) with vertices at \\( A = (0,0) \\), \\( B = (12,0) \\), and \\( C = (6, -6\\sqrt{3}) \\). The height of the prism is 16 units, so the top vertex \\( D \\) will be at \\( (6, -6\\sqrt{3} - 16) \\) and \\( E \\) and \\( F \\) will be directly above \\( A \\) and \\( C \\) respectively with distance 16 units.\n\nNext, we find the coordinates of \\( X \\), \\( Y \\), and \\( Z \\), which are the midpoints of \\( AC \\), \\( BC \\), and \\( DC \\) respectively.\n\nThe coordinates of \\( X \\), the midpoint of \\( AC \\), are:\n\\[\nX = \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right) = (3, -3\\sqrt{3})\n\\]\n\nThe coordinates of \\( Y \\), the midpoint of \\( BC \\), are:\n\\[\nY = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right) = (9, -3\\sqrt{3})\n\\]\n\nThe coordinates of \\( Z \\), the midpoint of \\( DC \\), are:\n\\[\nZ = \\left( \\frac{6+6}{2}, \\frac{-6\\sqrt{3}-6\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\right) = (6, -6\\sqrt{3})\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to calculate the side lengths of triangle \\(XYZ\\). Notice that points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) have the same coordinates. Therefore, the distance between any two of these points is the same.\n\nThe distance \\( XY \\) is:\n\\[\nXY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt{3})^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2} = 6\n\\]\n\nThe distance \\( XZ \\) is:\n\\[\nXZ = \\sqrt{(6-3)^2 + (-6\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt{3})^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 + (-3\\sqrt{3})^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 27} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n\\]\n\nThe distance \\( YZ \\) is:\n\\[\nYZ = \\sqrt{(6-9)^2 + (-6\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt{3})^2} = \\sqrt{(-3)^2 + (-3\\sqrt{3})^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 27} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n\\]\n\nSince all three sides of triangle \\(XYZ\\) are equal, triangle \\(XYZ\\) is an equilateral triangle with side length 6. The perimeter of an equilateral triangle is three times the side length:\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter} = 3 \\times 6 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
